  "body": {
    "id": "thm:joint-qte",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Under \\(\\text{ass:gamma-separation}\\) and the armwise learner and tuning hypotheses of \\(\\text{thm:oracle-preservation}\\) and the narrowed \\(\\text{thm:gaussian-branch}\\), along each subsequence with \\(\\ell_{a,n}\\to\\ell_a\\),\n\\[\n\\frac n{H_n}(\\widehat\\Delta^{\\rm bc}-\\Delta)\n\\Rightarrow \\ell_1L_1-\\ell_0L_0,\n\\]\nwhere \\(L_a=\\mathsf Z_{a,\\theta}/f_a\\) for \\(a\\in\\mathcal A_{\\rm H}\\), and \\(L_a\\) is the Gaussian vector generated by \\({\\rm IF}_a\\) for \\(a\\in\\mathcal A_{\\rm G}\\).  Unequal heavy indices are dominated by the smaller index, equal heavy indices retain both endpoint constants, a heavy arm dominates a finite-variance arm, and two finite-variance arms retain their shared learned-score covariance.  In the oracle-preserved two-heavy regime the endpoint processes are independent because their rare-event endpoint sets are disjoint.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\ell_{a,n}",
      "\\ell_a",
      "n",
      "H_n",
      "\\widehat\\Delta^{\\mathrm{bc}}",
      "\\Delta",
